WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.610
Week 9: Daily Routine and Reflexive Verbs. sequence a routine say what is happening now compare schedules

2
00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:20.108
Operational objective. By the end of this section you can sequence a routine, say what is happening now, compare schedules. The focus is useful performance, not isolated terminology.

3
00:00:20.108 --> 00:00:27.462
Language system. Reflexive pronouns; routines; antes de/después de; present progressive.

4
00:00:27.462 --> 00:00:33.557
Sound and delivery. Consonant clusters and the Spanish r after t, d, and b.

5
00:00:33.557 --> 00:00:43.090
Core principle. Notice meaning first, then form. Retrieve the new language aloud, compare it with the model, and repair one feature at a time.

6
00:00:43.090 --> 00:01:07.791
Model language. Me levanto a las seis y media. — I get up at six thirty. Después de vestirme, preparo el desayuno. — After getting dressed, I prepare breakfast. Ahora estoy esperando el tren. — I am waiting for the train now. Los niños se acuestan temprano. — The children go to bed early. ¿A qué hora te despiertas? — What time do you wake up?

7
00:01:07.791 --> 00:01:17.795
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
